{"kind":"assert","text":"G5 preparation found two concrete public-interface/authority design points before simulator wiring. (1) Public SDK has summary/device items and paged journal, but no capability-record query. Device targetAt alone misses older still-open commands. A bounded suffix scan needs a durable scan-through position in the application journal, advanced only through a head whose pending commands were all answered. Proposed demo-only simulator cursor item/act under grow.sense, expected revision fencing, through=the scanned head rather than marker entry; missing/incomplete coverage fails closed. This changes demo application data only, no host route or authority; no KV/private progress. (2) Sensors permission grow.sense cannot set vent/fan, raise alerts or close incidents (grow.climate), and being the operator's controlled agent does not grant those acts. Repeating incident count and actionable authorization therefore need a distinct climate principal. Proposed same small Worker with separately enrolled climate agent, own climate key secret and role, controlled by operator; sensors key remains only grow.sense plus native owner answer. No sensor permission broadening or heat authorization by an agent. Planner decision requested on these two points; pure clock/target simulation and signed cadence preparation can continue independently. Current landing-page slice3671c985b passed build invariant and local desktop/phone QA; hosted room navigation remains operator evidence."}